<p>Use the following procedure to adjust the printable area.</p>
<ol>
<li><p>Open the printing preferences dialog box after 
 creating a document in an application.</p></li>
<li><p>Click the <span class="Term-Soft">2 Sided/Layout/Booklet</span> 
 menu on the <span class="Term-Soft">Detailed Settings</span> tab.</p></li>
<li><p>Select the type of draw area in the <span class="Term-Soft">Printable 
 Area:</span> list.</p></li>
</ol>
<div class="help-step-extra">
<ul>
<li><p class="Normal-indent">If you select 
 <span class="Term-Soft">Maximum</span>, print inside the 5 mm (0.2 inches) 
 margin around the paper edges, the quality might be reduced.</p></li>
</ul>
</div>
<ol start="4">
<li><p>After making any other necessary settings, click 
 <span class="Term-OS">OK</span> to close the printing preferences dialog 
 box.</p></li>
<li><p>Start printing.</p></li>
</ol>
<h2>Adjusting the Print Image on the Paper</h2>
<p>Use the following procedure to adjust the image position.</p>
<ol>
<li><p>Open the printing preferences dialog box after 
 creating a document in an application.</p></li>
<li><p>Click the <span class="Term-Soft">2 Sided/Layout/Booklet</span> 
 menu on the <span class="Term-Soft">Detailed Settings</span> tab.</p></li>
<li><p>Click <span class="Term-Soft">Set Image Position...</span> 
 to open the <span class="Term-Soft">Set Image Position</span> dialog box.</p></li>
<li><p>Select the print position in the <span class="Term-Soft">Image 
 Position:</span> list.</p></li>
<li><p>In the <span class="Term-Soft">Adjust Image Position</span> 
 area, select the direction in which you want to shift the print area in 
 the <span class="Term-Soft">Direction:</span> list. Change the margins (top, 
 bottom, left, right) according to the selected direction.</p></li>
<li><p>Click <span class="Term-Soft">OK</span> to close 
 the dialog box.</p></li>
<li><p>After making any other necessary settings, click 
 <span class="Term-OS">OK</span> to close the printing preferences dialog 
 box.</p></li>
<li><p>Start printing.</p></li>
</ol>
